										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "**Auto-logout off:** the keep alive stops aborting the session. The session stays connected, and keeping its view up to date is up to you."
									},
									{
										"__type" : "textSnippet",
										"children" : {
											"__type" : "snippets",
											"items" : [ ]
										},
										"createEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"createTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-04T22:27:02.285953+01:00"
											}
										},
										"editEmail" : {
											"__type" : "email",
											"emailString" : "<unknown>"
										},
										"editTime" : {
											"__type" : "time",
											"time" : {
												"__type" : "dateAndTime",
												"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-04T22:27:02.285953+01:00"
											}
										},
										"uid" : {
											"__type" : "uid",
											"uidString" : "cdySjTtGTB+0/wV1NpNr/g=="
										},
										"paragraphStyle" : {
											"__type" : "textStyle"
										},
										"string" : "**Auto-logout on:** the session is logged out. The logout is announced one poll in advance ({{gtMethod:GtGemStoneKeepAliveSession>>#updateLogoutStateForNextPollIn:}}): the session shows up in orange in the notification and in the session lists, as *logout pending*. From there you can log it out right away or, if the connector allows it, postpone the logout (by default for 15 minutes, {{gtMethod:GtGemStoneGciConnector class>>#defaultLogoutPostponeDuration}}). Note that a session is logged out even if it has uncommitted changes; those changes are lost."
									}
								]
							},
